        <history>
          <p>This orchestral interlude from Delius's opera A Village Romeo and Juliet accompanies the two young lovers' final walk before their deaths, and has become far better known as a standalone concert piece than the opera itself. Its rich, slowly unfolding orchestration is frequently cited as one of the most representative examples of Delius's mature style.</p>
